# The only image built with the repository root as its context is `jekyll`
# (see _env/docker-compose.yml), and its Dockerfile copies just the Gemfile
# pair. Excluding everything else keeps the build context from shipping the
# whole ~2.8G working tree to the daemon.
#
# The site itself is bind-mounted at runtime, not COPYed, so nothing here
# affects what Jekyll actually renders.
*
!Gemfile
!Gemfile.lock
